The '''Namara''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed in [[the galaxy]]. [[Silvasu Fi]], [[Wini Eres]], and [[Xonr]] were all notable members of this species.

==Biology and appearance==
The Namara<ref name="Instapost">{{Instagram|username=jakeluntdavies|url=p/CjBPfCgKnOL|name=[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2022-09-28|quote=Background Aliens in Andor #002. This holo-dancer in episode 1 of Andor was an alien species I'd originally designed for the casino in TLJ (➡️2). Other versions appeared in Solo as cloud rider Silvasu Fi (➡️3) and hanging out with Lando at a Sabaac game (➡️4). In the Mandalorian you can see one at the Gamorrean fight (➡️5) and another making shady deals on the streets (➡️6). The only sketch I have to share is this (➡️5) featuring one I did for TROS. Despite a now healthy outing in the SW galaxy, her species still remains nameless 🙁 Maybe I'm wrong - help me out @holocronkeeper|archivefile=File:JakeDaviesNamara.png}} (response by [[Leland Chee]] ([https://instagram.com/holocronkeeper @holocronkeeper]) (comment on September 28, 2022): {{C|"We passed along a bunch of species names for the Galaxy's Edge Datapad app. This one we were calling Namara."}}</ref> were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] distinguished by their [[Color|black]] [[eye]]s and downward-turning horns that extended from the sides of their heads.<ref name="TLJ" />

==In the galaxy==
During the [[Imperial Era]], [[Silvasu Fi]], a member of the species, served the [[Cloud-Riders]] as they stole supplies from the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] and [[Crimson Dawn]] in an effort to fuel a [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebellion]].<ref name="Solo" /> Another Namara, the [[bounty hunter]] [[Xonr]], worked for the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] and tracked down the rogue hunter [[Beilert Valance]] in an attempt to eliminate him, but was killed by the [[cyborg]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Target Vader 1" />

During the [[New Republic era]] in [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mando Date">{{MandoDate}}</ref> a member of the species was present on [[Nevarro]], walking by the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]]<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> and later chatting with a fellow [[human]].<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> When Din Djarin and [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] were searching for [[Jedi]] to reunite the Child with its kind, a Namara could be seen amongst an audience watching a pair of [[Gamorrean]]s fight.<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref>

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="TLJ Date">{{FilmDate|VIII}}</ref> at least two [[Gender|female]] Namaras were present on [[Canto Bight]] during [[Rose Tico]] and [[Finn]]'s [[Mission to Canto Bight|search]] for the [[Master Codebreaker]]. One walked by [[Dobbu Scay]] and the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] as the former attempted to use the [[droid]] as a [[slot machine]].<ref name="TLJ" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:JakeDaviesNamara.png|thumb|right|250px|Jake Davies' instagram post]]
The species made their debut in the [[2017]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']], directed by [[Rian Johnson]].<ref name="TLJ" /> Artist [[Jake Lunt Davies]] designed the species for the film and revealed as such in an post on Instagram. Though he himself was unaware of the species' name, or if it had been named, [[Leland Chee]] responded and advised that they had named the species "Namara". This name was provided to the developers of [[Star Wars: Datapad]],<ref name="Instapost" /> a [[2019]] mobile game for use in [[Disneyland]], though it did not get used in the final product.<ref name="Datapad">[[Star Wars: Datapad|''Star Wars'': Datapad]]</ref>

